---
import InfoPage from '../../components/InfoPage.astro';

// Wording is carried over from the live page (last updated April 25, 2025), unchanged.
// Change from the live page: the meta description said "work accident and illness cases"; "illness"
// is removed (owner's rule: no work illness content anywhere).
// Updated Oct 28, 2026 from "Privacy Policy Update - 10-28-26.docx" (Bryn's approved decisions).
// Added: website contact form, attorney-client notice, retention, Cloudflare Turnstile (with the link
// Cloudflare requires), Cloudflare Web Analytics, cookies, both offices. All SMS sections are unchanged
// except "Sharing Your Information" (one sentence added) and the intro and Contact Us.
// BEFORE LAUNCH: replace [DATE TO BE SET AT LAUNCH] with the real date; confirm Web Analytics is
// switched on in Cloudflare (the page says it is); check the live site's cookies once after launch.
// The contact email below was hidden by the old site's spam protection and was read from its page source.
const title = 'Privacy Policy - Pathfinder Injury Law';
const description =
  'Pathfinder Injury Law helps in Virginia work accident cases. View our privacy policy or contact us for a consultation.';
---
<InfoPage title={title} description={description} path="/privacy-policy/" h1="Privacy Policy">
  <p>
    We prioritize Your confidentiality and privacy. This privacy policy, last updated on [DATE TO BE
    SET AT LAUNCH], explains how We collect, use, disclose, and protect Your information when You use
    our website, including our contact form, and concerning SMS (Short Message Service) messaging
    through 10DLC to enable effective communication between You and Us.
  </p>

  <h2>Our Website and Contact Form</h2>
  <p>Our website has a contact form. If You use it, We collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name;</li>
    <li>Your email address;</li>
    <li>Your phone number;</li>
    <li>The message You write; and</li>
    <li>Your confirmation that You understand sending the form does not create an attorney-client relationship.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use this information to read and respond to Your inquiry. Each message is saved in a database
    hosted by Cloudflare, and a copy is emailed to two inboxes at Pathfinder Injury Law. Those emails
    are sent through Google Workspace. Please do not send confidential or sensitive information through this website. Messages sent this way are not inherently secure.
  </p>
  <p>
    The contact form does not store Your IP address. Cloudflare, which hosts our website, may keep its
    own technical records of requests to the site, such as the page requested and the time.
  </p>

  <h2>Sending Us an Inquiry</h2>
  <p>
    Sending an inquiry through this website, or by phone, email, or text, does not create an
    attorney-client relationship. Please do not send confidential or sensitive information through this website. Messages sent this way are not inherently secure. If You need
    to reach Us about something urgent, call <a href="tel:+18045050633">(804) 505-0633</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How Long We Keep Contact Form Messages</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Messages from people who may need our help, and messages Our system is not sure about, are kept in our database as long as We reasonably need them.</li>
    <li>Messages that Our system identifies as spam or automated are deleted from the database after 90 days.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Bot Protection (Cloudflare Turnstile)</h2>
  <p>
    To keep automated spam out, Our contact form uses Cloudflare Turnstile, a bot check provided by
    Cloudflare, Inc. Turnstile runs in the background when You use the form. You are not asked to solve
    a puzzle. To tell people from bots, Turnstile receives limited technical information from Your
    browser, such as Your IP address, browser type, and the website it is running on. Cloudflare
    handles that information under the
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare Turnstile Privacy Addendum</a>
    and its general Privacy Policy. Our website receives only the result of the check, whether it
    passed or not, and not the technical information Turnstile collects. We keep that result with
    the message.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Our website uses Cloudflare Web Analytics to see how many people visit and which pages they read.
    Cloudflare has described this service as not using cookies and not tracking individual visitors
    across sites. We use this only to understand and improve the site.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare Turnstile may use browser storage or cookies that Cloudflare describes as strictly
    necessary to detect bots. Apart from those, We do not use cookies on this website.
  </p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>When You opt-in to receive SMS messages from Us, We may collect the following types of information:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Personal Information: Name, phone number, and email address (if provided);</li>
    <li>Case-Related Information: case number and client ID (if applicable);</li>
    <li>Relevant details necessary for effective communication regarding Your case; and</li>
    <li>Message Data: The content of SMS messages sent and received, delivery status of SMS messages, and interaction data related to SMS messages.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <p>We use the collected information strictly for case management and communication purposes, specifically for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Communication: Providing case updates, obtaining information, sending and receiving photos and files, and responding to client inquiries and delivering necessary legal support via SMS.</li>
    <li>Service Improvement: Understanding and analyzing the use of our SMS services and improving communication methods to better serve clients.</li>
    <li>Legal Compliance: Complying with applicable laws and regulations and responding to lawful requests and legal processes</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Sharing Your Information</h2>
  <p>We will never sell Your information to anyone ever. We may share or disclose Your information to third parties as necessary in the following cases:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Service Providers: We may share Your information with trusted third-party service providers that assist us in operating our firm, such as case management systems and SMS services. These parties are required to maintain the confidentiality and security of your information. For our website contact form, these providers include Cloudflare (website hosting, database, and bot check) and Google (Google Workspace email).</li>
    <li>Third-Party Counsel and Referral Attorneys: We may share Your information with trusted third-party counsel and attorneys to whom We refer You, if You authorize Us to do so.</li>
    <li>Legal Requirements: We may disclose Your information if required by law or in response to a valid legal request such as a subpoena, court order, or government demand.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Security of Your Information</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable measures to protect Your information from unauthorized access, disclosure,
    alteration, or destruction. However, no method of transmission over the Internet or electronic
    storage is 100% secure, and We cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>Your Rights and Choices</h2>
  <p>You have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Opt-Out: You can opt out of receiving SMS messages from Us by replying “STOP” to any message, or by contacting Us at any of the methods set out in the “Contact Us” section below.</li>
    <li>Access and Correction: You can request access to or correction of Your personal information by contacting Us at any of the methods set out in the “Contact Us” section below.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be effective when We post
    the revised policy on Our website. We encourage You to review this Privacy Policy periodically.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact Us</h2>
  <p>If You have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy or Our privacy practices, you may contact Us by any of the following methods:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>By phone: <a href="tel:+18045050633">(804) 505-0633</a></li>
    <li>By email: <a href="mailto:admin@pathfinderlaw.com">admin@pathfinderlaw.com</a></li>
    <li>
      By mail, or in person by appointment, at either office (the mailing address is the same as the office address):
      <ul>
        <li>Richmond office: Pathfinder Injury Law, 8010 Ridge Road, Suite A, Richmond, VA 23229</li>
        <li>Chincoteague office: Pathfinder Injury Law, 6294 Cropper Street, Chincoteague, Virginia 23336</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>
</InfoPage>
